From 729bdc3bbbc9c4cb1fc2ca1ffeac92ea7d551383 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jupiter Belic <belikh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:30:45 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] irix7: run pthreads on the cooperative thread gate

Give the IRIX 7 PAL a real pthread layer.  The kernel thread pointer ($28)
still points at the 16-byte ABI header; relibc's Tcb and Pthread records are
appended after it, both for the main thread in crt0's BSS and for workers
mapped by Tcb::new.  pthread_self and __errno_location read $28, and every
thread gets its own key map, cleanup list, thread-exit handlers and errno.

pthread_create keeps relibc's existing stack-frame contract and maps
SYS_THREAD_CREATE through rlct_clone, recording the returned kernel tid in
the new Pthread before the creator can yield.  pthread_join waits on the
thread's libc-owned exit word with futex_wait; the worker posts its start
routine's return value and retires with SYS_THREAD_EXIT.  A joined worker's
TCB and stack are released; a detached thread can only drop its table entry
because it is still running on that stack.

sched_yield and exit_thread map to the native thread calls, and gettid now
reads the current thread's tid instead of returning the process id.  The
mutex owner word therefore differs per thread, so the existing RlctMutex
fast path and futex contention path work across threads.  The default stack
for this target drops to 64 KiB because the kernel's anonymous heap is a
fixed 1 MiB shared with the allocator.

Refs irix7/os#318.

Signed-off-by: Jupiter Belic <belikh@users.noreply.github.com>
